You said: It tells me which kind of list gets built when filter or map makes a new one, and by default it points back to the plain list maker itself: asking for it on the built-in list returned the Array maker (length 1). For my own special list I want filter and map to hand back my special kind, and only if I override this to point at the plain maker would I get a plain list back.
Their question: When you actually change which kind of list comes back, what is the real situation that makes you do it, for example a special list that keeps extra info where you want filter or map to give you a plain list so the extra info doesn't get carried along?

